NapSAT logo and brand assets
============================

Copyright (c) 2026 Robin Coutelier
Designed by beamoonforge

The NapSAT logo was created by the artist beamoonforge, who assigned all rights
in the artwork to Robin Coutelier in 2026. beamoonforge remains the author of
the design and must be credited as its designer wherever the authorship of the
artwork is stated.

The contents of this directory -- the NapSAT logo in all its forms, including
the TikZ sources (logo-common.tex, Logo.tex, Logo
Dark.tex) and every rendering of them (Logo.*, Logo-Dark.*), -- are NOT covered by the MIT license that applies to the
rest of NapSAT. They are licensed under the terms below.


What you may do
---------------

You may copy, display, and redistribute the logo, unmodified, in order to refer
to the NapSAT project. This is expressly encouraged in, for example:

  * academic papers, talks, posters, and slides that discuss or cite NapSAT;
  * documentation, README files, and websites of software that uses NapSAT;
  * competition submissions, benchmarks, and evaluations that include NapSAT;
  * lists of tools, dependencies, package indices, and similar catalogues;
  * teaching material and news coverage about NapSAT.

Such use requires no permission and no fee, in any medium, including commercial
ones, for as long as the logo is being used to refer to NapSAT.

Wherever the authorship of the logo is stated, credit the designer:

    NapSAT logo by beamoonforge.


What you may not do
-------------------

Anything else requires written permission from the copyright holder. In
particular, you may not:

  * use the logo for any purpose other than referring to NapSAT, whether
    decoratively or as general-purpose artwork detached from the project;
  * use it as the logo, icon, avatar, or identifying mark of another project,
    product, organisation, or fork;
  * use it in a way that suggests that the NapSAT project endorses, sponsors,
    or is affiliated with your project, product, or organisation;
  * sell it, or sell merchandise bearing it;
  * distribute modified versions of it.

Recolouring, cropping, redrawing, stretching, and combining the logo with other
marks all count as modification. If you need a variant -- a monochrome version
for print, a different aspect ratio, an icon-only crop -- please ask rather than
making one yourself. The official variants in this directory are produced by the
copyright holder, and more can be added.


The name "NapSAT"
-----------------

This license covers copyright in the artwork only. It grants no rights in the
name "NapSAT" or in the logo used as a mark, and the same principle applies to
both: you may use the name to refer to the project, but not as the name of a
fork or a derived work. Forks are welcome under the MIT license that covers the
code, but they should carry their own name and their own logo.


Requests
--------

For any use not permitted above, contact Robin Coutelier
<robin.coutelier@tuwien.ac.at>.
